This arXiv source package contains the manuscript *Breaking the HBM
wall: A Distributed Spatial Processing-Near-Memory Architecture using
DUV ASICs and Deterministic Routing* and its figures, both under
CC BY-SA 4.0. The full text of the license is available at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

The open-hardware artifacts that back the paper (Verilog RTL, the Go
co-simulation harness, the C firmware, the PCB designs and the
cross-compilation toolchains) are published separately under the
three-way license split documented in the artifact repository's
LICENSE file (CERN-OHL-S v2 for the HDL, AGPL-3.0 for the harness
and firmware).
